csv - Unix-style commands for CSV files
=======================================

csv is a collection of Unix-style utilities for working with CSV files on a
row basis rather than a line basis. This properly handles CSV files with
quoted fields that may contain newlines or commas.

Commands
--------

  * csv head - Display the first n data rows
  * csv tail - Display the last n data rows
  * csv wc   - Count rows, columns, and bytes
  * csv cut  - Select specific fields by name

Features
--------

  * Row-aware parsing: correctly handles quoted fields with embedded newlines
  * Comment support: preserves leading # comment lines
  * Consistent interface: -a flag adds header across all commands
  * Pipeline friendly: reads from stdin when no file specified
  * GNU-style options: familiar command-line interface

Installation
------------

    make install

Or to install to a custom location:

    make install prefix=$HOME/.local

Requirements
------------

  * Python 3.6 or later
  * No external dependencies (uses only Python standard library)

Usage Examples
--------------

    # Show first 5 data rows
    csv head -5 data.csv

    # Show last 3 rows with header
    csv tail -3 -a data.csv

    # Count data rows
    csv wc -l data.csv

    # Select specific columns
    csv cut -f data.csv name email phone

    # Pipeline: filter then select
    csv head -10 -a data.csv | csv cut -a name city

Documentation
-------------

See the man page for complete documentation:

    man csv

